  "notes": "\"Minor, low\" is the first thing the research says about the keys and it is the parameter that separates this from every other G-Unit-adjacent entry: `melody.register` [58,80], the lowest lead register in this batch. \"Tight and dry\" is a narrow `velocityTiers` spread plus a single rim perc lane; \"snare rolls into hooks\" is `fills.snareRollLadder` true. The occasional Phrygian synth lead is `halfStepDissonance` 0.1 and a phrygian scale at weight 2, not a chord family, because the research puts it on the lead. The sustained sub on the tonic is `mirror_kick` at 0.94 — the engine's held-note rhythm saturates, and a root on each kick over a 1-and-3& pattern is the nearest honest reading. ⚠ `medium`. The i–VII family at weight 2 is a REDUCTION of the researched i–VI–VII, and the research's own note is that the label sound is covered by the separate `50 Cent / G-Unit era` entry — so what is Banks-specific here is the low register and the dryness, and the rest is the G-Unit bed around him.",
